<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20859" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hŏmērŏmastix</span></b> ,
			īgis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὁμηρομάστιξ</span> (Homer's scourge), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>the censurer of Homer.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, an epithet given to the critic Zoilus,
				<i><span class="en">Vitr. 7 praef.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in gen., <i>a
				censorious person</i>: ut obiter caveam istos Homeromastigas,
			etc., Plin. H. N. praef. § 28.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
